{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00944",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.75,
      "end_seconds": 15.35,
      "duration_seconds": 14.6,
      "text": "Hi, um, so, I'm kind of embarrassed to say this, but I leak a little when I laugh or sneeze. Ever since the baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.65,
      "end_seconds": 25.1,
      "duration_seconds": 8.45,
      "text": "Thanks for telling me, nothing to be embarrassed about. How old is the baby? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.99,
      "end_seconds": 31.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "Three months. Little guy's a monster. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.96,
      "end_seconds": 38.0,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "Three months, so about three months of leaking, then?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.6,
      "end_seconds": 51.58,
      "duration_seconds": 10.98,
      "text": "Yeah, about that. It started when I got back to the gym, actually. I jumped on the box and, oops."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.08,
      "end_seconds": 61.24,
      "duration_seconds": 7.16,
      "text": "What's a typical leak look like? A drop or a lot? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.83,
      "end_seconds": 72.02,
      "duration_seconds": 8.19,
      "text": "A little squirt, not a flood. Enough that I have to change my underwear. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.85,
      "end_seconds": 79.61,
      "duration_seconds": 6.76,
      "text": "And does it happen when you laugh, cough, or jump? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.78,
      "end_seconds": 89.06,
      "duration_seconds": 8.28,
      "text": "All of those. Laughing at my husband's jokes, mostly, which is not often. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.43,
      "end_seconds": 99.49,
      "duration_seconds": 8.06,
      "text": "Do you feel the urge to go and then not make it in time? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.91,
      "end_seconds": 108.34,
      "duration_seconds": 6.43,
      "text": "Not really. It's only when I do something, like sneeze. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.54,
      "end_seconds": 113.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Any burning when you pee?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.77,
      "end_seconds": 117.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "No burning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.47,
      "end_seconds": 123.85,
      "duration_seconds": 5.38,
      "text": "How often do you go during the day? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.68,
      "end_seconds": 132.0,
      "duration_seconds": 7.32,
      "text": "Normal, I think. Every few hours. I'm too busy to notice. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.61,
      "end_seconds": 140.57,
      "duration_seconds": 6.96,
      "text": "Are you taking anything for it, or anything else I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.41,
      "end_seconds": 149.49,
      "duration_seconds": 8.08,
      "text": "Just a prenatal vitamin, one a day. I'm breastfeeding, so I keep taking it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.36,
      "end_seconds": 163.28,
      "duration_seconds": 12.92,
      "text": "That's fine. Now, let me explain what's going on in plain English. Imagine the muscles at the bottom of your pelvis as a hammock. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.36,
      "end_seconds": 167.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "A hammock, okay. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.01,
      "end_seconds": 184.29,
      "duration_seconds": 15.28,
      "text": "Pregnancy and delivery stretch the hammock. When you cough or jump, the pressure goes down, and a stretched hammock can't hold it back as well. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.01,
      "end_seconds": 193.37,
      "duration_seconds": 8.36,
      "text": "That makes sense. It feels like I can't squeeze like I used to. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.88,
      "end_seconds": 202.16,
      "duration_seconds": 7.28,
      "text": "Right. And the good news is that hammocks can be tightened up with training. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 203.74,
      "end_seconds": 207.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Like a workout for down there? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.26,
      "end_seconds": 222.05,
      "duration_seconds": 11.79,
      "text": "Exactly. Squeeze as though you're stopping the flow of urine, hold for five seconds, then relax. Do ten of those, three times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 223.63,
      "end_seconds": 227.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "Can I do that in the car? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.22,
      "end_seconds": 237.65,
      "duration_seconds": 8.43,
      "text": "Anywhere. Nobody can tell. Many people find it easiest while waiting at a red light. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 239.83,
      "end_seconds": 245.74,
      "duration_seconds": 5.91,
      "text": "I'll do it at every red light, then. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.41,
      "end_seconds": 259.74,
      "duration_seconds": 12.33,
      "text": "Empty your bladder before you exercise, and be gentle at the gym for a while. Skip the box jumps for now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 261.9,
      "end_seconds": 265.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "Oh, that's the sad part. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.33,
      "end_seconds": 275.69,
      "duration_seconds": 7.36,
      "text": "It's only for a while. Try to build it up slowly. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 276.8,
      "end_seconds": 280.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "Okay, okay. And that's it? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.51,
      "end_seconds": 290.66,
      "duration_seconds": 9.15,
      "text": "There are other options, too, if the exercises don't do enough, but give this a real go first. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 293.23,
      "end_seconds": 299.14,
      "duration_seconds": 5.91,
      "text": "Fair enough. Does it matter if I'm nursing? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 300.91,
      "end_seconds": 304.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "Not for the exercises. They're safe. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 305.74,
      "end_seconds": 308.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "Great. Thanks, doctor. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.66,
      "end_seconds": 313.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "You're welcome. Enjoy the monster. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 314.95,
      "end_seconds": 317.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "Ha, will do. ~"
    }
  ]
}
